### F12 — `_weighted_cluster_center` counts only `{-1, -2}` as outlier labels
severity: medium
evidence: sklearn/cluster/_hdbscan/hdbscan.py:894-895 — `# Number of non-noise clusters / n_clusters = len(set(self.labels_) - {-1, -2})`. `_OUTLIER_ENCODING` defines three outlier labels: `-1` (noise), `-2` (infinite), `-3` (missing) (lines 65-79 and class docstring lines 534-537).
scenario: user with missing (`np.nan`) samples calls `fit` with `store_centers="centroid"` → `n_clusters` is over-counted by 1, `self.centroids_` is allocated with one extra row that is never written (contains uninitialized memory from `np.empty`) and the loop over `range(n_clusters)` iterates past the true cluster count, hitting an empty `data[mask]` and producing warnings / NaN centroids for the phantom cluster index.
contract: Compute `n_clusters = len(set(self.labels_) - {-1, -2, -3})` (or subtract `{lbl for _, o in _OUTLIER_ENCODING.items() for lbl in [o["label"]]} | {-1}`).
